<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel jumps above SGB offer price.</title>
<headline>Tractebel jumps above SGB offer price.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian utility holding company Tractebel surged five percent to 14,800 francs per share, well above the 14,500 francs offer price from Societe Generale de Belgique (SGB), at the market opening on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It then continued to climb to 14,850 francs.</p>
<p>SGB announced after the close of business on Tuesday it had agreed to raise its stake in Tractebel to 65 percent from 40 at a price of 14,500 francs per share, and launch an offer for the remainder at the same price.</p>
<p>The 25 percent chunk it bought on Tuesday was held by Electrafina and insurer Royale Belge.</p>
<p>Electrafina rose 45 francs to 2,895 and Royale Belge climbed 40 francs to 5,970.</p>
